Model Card: Adaptive Surrogate-Based BBO Strategy
1. Overview

Name: Adaptive Multi-Surrogate Black-Box Optimisation Strategy
Type: Surrogate-based black-box optimisation framework
Version: Final Capstone Submission (Week 10)

This model describes a flexible Black-Box Optimisation (BBO) strategy developed for the Imperial College London ML Capstone project. The approach is not a single fixed model, but an adaptive framework that selects different surrogate models and acquisition strategies depending on the dimensionality, noise level, and observed behaviour of each function.

Across the ten rounds, the strategy evolved from broad exploration to targeted exploitation, with method switching when progress plateaued.

